menu "KeyKeeper2 secure radio link (kkproto)"

    config KEYKEEPER_KKPROTO
        bool "Build the kkproto library (Noise XX/IK link to a radio dongle)"
        default n
        help
            Builds components/kkproto: the portable protocol library for the encrypted link
            between the vault and a radio dongle (Noise XX pairing, Noise IK sessions, framing,
            messages, pairing code). It has no effect on the device until something calls it.

            Needs an mbedTLS configuration with X25519 (Curve25519), ChaCha20-Poly1305,
            SHA-256 and HMAC. kk::crypto::selftest() reports at run time if one is missing --
            call it once at boot of anything that uses the link.

            Off by default: nothing in the firmware depends on it yet.

endmenu
